      },
      "message": "fix(verify): name a cut deeper than the flute length first\n\nA 2D Pocket, Adaptive, Offset or Contour that cuts deeper below the\nstock top than its tool's flute length now says so first: a note with\nthe tool, the flute length and the depth, and, when the shank or holder\nlaws convict the body, the advisory warning flute_short before those\nfindings. The finding never holds the post; the shank and holder\nfindings do (the #3525 decision). The first form blocked a wider shank\nand refused the clean t31 contour program; it is dropped.\n\nFixes #3525\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
